# efi_display_without_newframe: An EFI present to a display without a new_frame callback asserts in DisplayCore::present_frame, and the host dies. Without trace callbacks the first timer tick presents. The death is on EFI's present queue, after the tick has queued mode_change to the display's queue, so the scenario ends in a wait only the death ends (0x102c never reads 2) rather than one for mode_change, which could return first.
{"displays": [{"handlers": ["modeChange"], "modes": [[64, 32, 60]], "name": "suite", "port": 0, "serial": 1000}], "op": "config", "ram": [["0x40000000", "0x4000000"]], "stamp_slots": 2, "watchdog_s": 30}
{"off": "0x1034", "op": "mmio_w", "val": "0xf5"}
{"off": "0x1200", "op": "mmio_w", "val": "0x1"}
{"off": "0x121c", "op": "mmio_w", "val": "0x80010"}
{"off": "0x1218", "op": "mmio_w", "val": "0x20"}
{"off": "0x1228", "op": "mmio_w", "val": "0x40"}
{"off": "0x1210", "op": "mmio_w", "val": "0x10002"}
{"off": "0x1214", "op": "mmio_w", "val": "0x4000"}
{"label": "the first tick: the host dies", "mmio": "0x102c", "mmio_eq": "0x2", "op": "wait", "timeout_ms": 10000}
